<section>
    <h3>The comment that changed the direction</h3>
    <blockquote class="review">
        We do want record and replay in HttpClient […]
        <b>build on what is already there instead of alongside it.</b>
        <br><br>
        None of this is a rejection of the idea. It is a request to make the recorder produce real HAR
        that our existing reader consumes, to <b>fail closed</b>, and to <b>keep secrets out of files people commit</b>.
        <cite>Nicolas Grekas, August 17, 2026</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>On August 17, Nicolas Grekas wrote this comment.</p>
        <p>In short: yes, we want this feature. But build on what exists. Real HAR files that Symfony can already read. Never go to the network by surprise. And no secrets in committed files.</p>
        <p>At first, this kind of comment hurts a little. But these three points are everything you saw today. This comment became the specification.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
